## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To enable the HTTP Gmail API, you will need 3 Google OAuth credentials in your `.env` and Render environment settings:
> 1. `GMAIL_CLIENT_ID` (from Google Cloud Console)
> 2. `GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET` (from Google Cloud Console)
> 3. `GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN` (generated via Google Developers OAuth Playground)
> 4. `GMAIL_USER` (e.g. `zeeshantahiralvi123@gmail.com`)
>
> Follow the 3-minute setup instructions below to generate these credentials.

### How to get your Google OAuth Credentials in 3 Minutes:
1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/) and create a project (or select an existing one).
2. Go to **APIs & Services > Library**, search for **Gmail API**, and click **Enable**.
3. Go to **APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen**:
   - Select **External**, set App Name (e.g. `PropPulse CRM`), and enter your email for user support and developer contact.
   - In **Test users**, add your own email (`zeeshantahiralvi123@gmail.com`).
4. Go to **APIs & Services > Credentials**:
   - Click **Create Credentials > OAuth client ID**.
   - Application type: **Web application**.
   - Name: `PropPulse CRM Gmail Client`.
   - Under **Authorized redirect URIs**, add: `https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground`.
   - Click **Create** and copy your **Client ID** and **Client Secret**.
5. Generate the **Refresh Token** using OAuth Playground:
   - Open [Google OAuth 2.0 Playground](https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground/).
   - Click the **Gear icon (OAuth 2.0 configuration)** in the top right:
     - Check **Use your own OAuth credentials**.
     - Paste your **OAuth Client ID** and **OAuth Client Secret**.
   - In Step 1 (Select & authorize APIs), find **Gmail API v1** and check `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send`.
   - Click **Authorize APIs** and log in with your Gmail account (`zeeshantahiralvi123@gmail.com`).
   - In Step 2, click **Exchange authorization code for tokens**.
   - Copy the resulting **Refresh token**.

